{
  "requirement": "No prompt, tool result, or tool error the harness gives the model MUST state a\nline number or line range of a project source, except within source text it\nquotes and where a tool error repeats a line number the model supplied. The\nharness MUST identify a source location by file and outline selector under\n{cite}`requirements.references.outline_selectors` instead.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.authoring.no_line_numbers`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. No tool result may state a line number or range of a project source. Quoted source text is exempt.\n2. No tool error may state one, except where it repeats a number the model supplied.\n3. No prompt may state one.\n4. Locations must be given by file and outline selector.\n\n**Tool results**\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs#mod[tests]/fn[reading_records_only_delivered_sources_and_their_terms]` asserts that `habeas` item reads and line-range reads carry no `line_start` or `line_end`. They return `fn[work]` selectors instead.\n- `fn[line_range_reads_record_the_innermost_covering_nodes]` asserts the same for Rust and plain-text line-range reads. Plain text is identified by `line@…` selectors. It also asserts that recorded inputs carry no line fields.\n- `fn[search_merges_context_windows_and_respects_ignore_rules]` and `fn[separate_windows_in_one_node_are_divided_by_an_elision_line]` assert that `ripgrep` entries and lines carry no `line_start` or `line` fields. They compare whole result shapes.\n- `fn[outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs]` asserts that `outline` entries carry only selectors, kinds and names.\n- `fn[references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs]` asserts exact `references` results, which contain file and item and no lines.\n- `src/sites.rs#mod[tests]/fn[sites_are_the_innermost_nodes_of_site_matches_and_violations_within_them]` asserts the model-facing match value has only `kind`, `query`, `item` and `text`. The internal `line_start` is not exposed.\n\n**Tool errors**\n- `src/authoring/line_numbers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_drop_the_source_line_of_a_parse_error]` covers each error form unit by unit:\n  - parse-error line prefixes;\n  - file-and-line diagnostics;\n  - a duplicate-declaration error's second file-and-line reference;\n  - YAML line-and-column positions;\n  - TOML position text.\n  \n  Each is rewritten to `file#`. It also asserts that single-line and range forms from `read_lines` are kept unchanged, which is the exception for numbers the model supplied.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[tool_errors_give_the_model_no_line_numbers_it_did_not_supply]` is an end-to-end test. An out-of-range request error still repeats the number the model gave. A parse error on a broken file does contain a line number when raised by the tool. The error delivered to the model in the next request contains `cannot parse` and no line-number text. The conversation `dispatch` routes every tool error through `without_source_lines`.\n\n**Prompts and locations by selector**\n- `fn[site_reviews_use_their_prompt_and_record_applies_and_the_site]` asserts the site prompt names the site by file and selector. It asserts exact equality with the approved template filled with selector-only matches and mandatory inputs.\n- `src/authoring/inputs.rs#mod[tests]/fn[anchored_files_contribute_root_node_inputs]` asserts the mandatory inputs by exact equality. They carry file, item and hash only.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[submission_description_tests]/fn[submission_descriptions_explain_arguments_and_successful_completion]` asserts the submit tool descriptions tell the model to use \"outline selectors, never line numbers\".\n\n**Gaps**\nI found none. Every obligation has a test that exercises it and asserts the outcome. The exception for numbers the model supplied is tested in both its single-line and range forms. No acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "5f07d59d3d70ca6a503110d2a797133c2b9f1eafd54fb53e7ee2fb02587ec51a",
